n/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x+6)(x-4)$ is $x=${{field-1}}."] ["question-4cf4852d-d3c2-5b9a-829d-615cf17e0f68" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=-(x+6)(x-4),$ we can tell that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-6$ and ${x}_{2}=4.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6+4}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-2)}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-1.$"] ["question-4cf4852d-d3c2-5b9a-829d-615cf17e0f68" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b93cd0f2-3775-53e1-8100-fdd69419df85" :answer-field/id #uuid "b93cd0f2-3775-53e1-8100-fdd69419df85"] ["answer-9e880c63-17e5-55ec-9752-a08e206ebf91" :answer/id #uuid "9e880c63-17e5-55ec-9752-a08e206ebf91"] ["answer-9e880c63-17e5-55ec-9752-a08e206ebf91" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9e880c63-17e5-55ec-9752-a08e206ebf91" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-field-b93cd0f2-3775-53e1-8100-fdd69419df85" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-b93cd0f2-3775-53e1-8100-fdd69419df85" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-b93cd0f2-3775-53e1-8100-fdd69419df85" :answer-field/correct "answer-9e880c63-17e5-55ec-9752-a08e206ebf91"] ["answer-field-b93cd0f2-3775-53e1-8100-fdd69419df85" :answer-field/choices "answer-9e880c63-17e5-55ec-9752-a08e206ebf91"] ["question-4cf4852d-d3c2-5b9a-829d-615cf17e0f68" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b93cd0f2-3775-53e1-8100-fdd69419df85"] [17592186110726 :knowledge-point/questions "question-4cf4852d-d3c2-5b9a-829d-615cf17e0f68"] ["question-cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0" :question/id #uuid "cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0"] ["question-cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-84902"] ["question-cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(6x-1)(3x+1).$"] ["question-cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=(6x-1)(3x+1),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=\\frac{1}{6}$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{2}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{1}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{12}.$"] ["question-cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/id #uuid "329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434"] ["answer-142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0" :answer/id #uuid "142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0"] ["answer-142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0" :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{12}"] ["answer-80b7f6d3-2e98-5ccb-856a-d66a6512df21" :answer/id #uuid "80b7f6d3-2e98-5ccb-856a-d66a6512df21"] ["answer-80b7f6d3-2e98-5ccb-856a-d66a6512df21" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-80b7f6d3-2e98-5ccb-856a-d66a6512df21" :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{4}"] ["answer-404a6d55-06c7-5863-9890-05c5ef448ad1" :answer/id #uuid "404a6d55-06c7-5863-9890-05c5ef448ad1"] ["answer-404a6d55-06c7-5863-9890-05c5ef448ad1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-404a6d55-06c7-5863-9890-05c5ef448ad1" :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{6}"] ["answer-169d9c2b-ed8e-5399-9665-91d1666641d3" :answer/id #uuid "169d9c2b-ed8e-5399-9665-91d1666641d3"] ["answer-169d9c2b-ed8e-5399-9665-91d1666641d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-169d9c2b-ed8e-5399-9665-91d1666641d3" :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{12}"] ["answer-29e329a9-3422-59f4-82ad-91d038159e57" :answer/id #uuid "29e329a9-3422-59f4-82ad-91d038159e57"] ["answer-29e329a9-3422-59f4-82ad-91d038159e57" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-29e329a9-3422-59f4-82ad-91d038159e57" :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{4}"] ["answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/correct "answer-142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0"] ["answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/choices "answer-142bb8d7-2c5b-5aff-a641-87db92de52c0"] ["answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/choices "answer-80b7f6d3-2e98-5ccb-856a-d66a6512df21"] ["answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/choices "answer-404a6d55-06c7-5863-9890-05c5ef448ad1"] ["answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/choices "answer-169d9c2b-ed8e-5399-9665-91d1666641d3"] ["answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434" :answer-field/choices "answer-29e329a9-3422-59f4-82ad-91d038159e57"] ["question-cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-329e691a-a395-50ed-b83a-cc3c4efd7434"] [17592186110726 :knowledge-point/questions "question-cd5e69ab-4017-5036-a080-1d135b13f5a0"] ["question-684d163d-4d1e-51cd-8879-d5e5b2f089b6" :question/id #uuid "684d163d-4d1e-51cd-8879-d5e5b2f089b6"] ["question-684d163d-4d1e-51cd-8879-d5e5b2f089b6" :question/math-academy-id "q-84906"] ["question-684d163d-4d1e-51cd-8879-d5e5b2f089b6" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(3x+4)(6x-k)$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ The value of $k=$"] ["question-684d163d-4d1e-51cd-8879-d5e5b2f089b6" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{3},$ we will set our result equal to $-\\frac{1}{3}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=-(3x+4)(6x-k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{4}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{k}{6}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{k}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{8}{6}+\\frac{k}{6})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{k-8}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{3}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k-8}{12} & =-\\frac{1}{3} \\\\ k-8 & =-4 \\\\ k & =-4+8 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-684d163d-4d1e-51cd-8879-d5e5b2f089b6" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/id #uuid "6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8"] ["answer-1c7dd35c-387e-5c8f-8d52-8df49f54ba91" :answer/id #uuid "1c7dd35c-387e-5c8f-8d52-8df49f54ba91"] ["answer-1c7dd35c-387e-5c8f-8d52-8df49f54ba91" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-1c7dd35c-387e-5c8f-8d52-8df49f54ba91" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-f26ad368-7367-5130-8843-f17ee8749540" :answer/id #uuid "f26ad368-7367-5130-8843-f17ee8749540"] ["answer-f26ad368-7367-5130-8843-f17ee8749540" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-f26ad368-7367-5130-8843-f17ee8749540" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-2231137b-d7d1-5097-a668-5b88fce4d605" :answer/id #uuid "2231137b-d7d1-5097-a668-5b88fce4d605"] ["answer-2231137b-d7d1-5097-a668-5b88fce4d605" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-2231137b-d7d1-5097-a668-5b88fce4d605" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-96e7ced7-ae8e-524c-9f9a-e5c32bd8d7a4" :answer/id #uuid "96e7ced7-ae8e-524c-9f9a-e5c32bd8d7a4"] ["answer-96e7ced7-ae8e-524c-9f9a-e5c32bd8d7a4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-96e7ced7-ae8e-524c-9f9a-e5c32bd8d7a4" :answer/value "8"] ["answer-8240c150-e4cb-507a-8888-b6ef07b60c64" :answer/id #uuid "8240c150-e4cb-507a-8888-b6ef07b60c64"] ["answer-8240c150-e4cb-507a-8888-b6ef07b60c64" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-8240c150-e4cb-507a-8888-b6ef07b60c64" :answer/value "9"] ["answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/correct "answer-f26ad368-7367-5130-8843-f17ee8749540"] ["answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-1c7dd35c-387e-5c8f-8d52-8df49f54ba91"] ["answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-f26ad368-7367-5130-8843-f17ee8749540"] ["answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-2231137b-d7d1-5097-a668-5b88fce4d605"] ["answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-96e7ced7-ae8e-524c-9f9a-e5c32bd8d7a4"] ["answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8" :answer-field/choices "answer-8240c150-e4cb-507a-8888-b6ef07b60c64"] ["question-684d163d-4d1e-51cd-8879-d5e5b2f089b6" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-6a445e9b-2feb-5651-8789-3201593291a8"] [17592186110727 :knowledge-point/questions "question-684d163d-4d1e-51cd-8879-d5e5b2f089b6"] ["question-143580a6-1bb7-5c0f-bc9f-072a4a4b0e12" :question/id #uuid "143580a6-1bb7-5c0f-bc9f-072a4a4b0e12"] ["question-143580a6-1bb7-5c0f-bc9f-072a4a4b0e12" :question/math-academy-id "q-106169"] ["question-143580a6-1bb7-5c0f-bc9f-072a4a4b0e12" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of $y=(x-2k)(x+3k)$ is $x=-2.$ The value of $k=$"] ["question-143580a6-1bb7-5c0f-bc9f-072a4a4b0e12" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-2,$ we will set our result equal to $-2.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=(x-2k)(x+3k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=2k$ and ${x}_{2}=-3k.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2k+(-3k)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-k}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-2.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{-k}{2} & =-2 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-143580a6-1bb7-5c0f-bc9f-072a4a4b0e12" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/id #uuid "70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23"] ["answer-39ae4953-ea9c-5671-8840-4018a5578e01" :answer/id #uuid "39ae4953-ea9c-5671-8840-4018a5578e01"] ["answer-39ae4953-ea9c-5671-8840-4018a5578e01" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-39ae4953-ea9c-5671-8840-4018a5578e01" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-6669511f-d4ef-5505-b173-a7475fbc1511" :answer/id #uuid "6669511f-d4ef-5505-b173-a7475fbc1511"] ["answer-6669511f-d4ef-5505-b173-a7475fbc1511" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-6669511f-d4ef-5505-b173-a7475fbc1511" :answer/value "2"] ["answer-c9f335a4-a3ee-545c-8578-89d25b02d49d" :answer/id #uuid "c9f335a4-a3ee-545c-8578-89d25b02d49d"] ["answer-c9f335a4-a3ee-545c-8578-89d25b02d49d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-c9f335a4-a3ee-545c-8578-89d25b02d49d" :answer/value "3"] ["answer-b7e4b322-e190-5f51-8844-56c6bf60ae9b" :answer/id #uuid "b7e4b322-e190-5f51-8844-56c6bf60ae9b"] ["answer-b7e4b322-e190-5f51-8844-56c6bf60ae9b" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b7e4b322-e190-5f51-8844-56c6bf60ae9b" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-9e91fbe8-a391-5c1a-b5f5-c38ffbd44c43" :answer/id #uuid "9e91fbe8-a391-5c1a-b5f5-c38ffbd44c43"] ["answer-9e91fbe8-a391-5c1a-b5f5-c38ffbd44c43" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9e91fbe8-a391-5c1a-b5f5-c38ffbd44c43" :answer/value "6"] ["answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/correct "answer-b7e4b322-e190-5f51-8844-56c6bf60ae9b"] ["answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/choices "answer-39ae4953-ea9c-5671-8840-4018a5578e01"] ["answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/choices "answer-6669511f-d4ef-5505-b173-a7475fbc1511"] ["answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/choices "answer-c9f335a4-a3ee-545c-8578-89d25b02d49d"] ["answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/choices "answer-b7e4b322-e190-5f51-8844-56c6bf60ae9b"] ["answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23" :answer-field/choices "answer-9e91fbe8-a391-5c1a-b5f5-c38ffbd44c43"] ["question-143580a6-1bb7-5c0f-bc9f-072a4a4b0e12" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-70fe4864-23f4-51f6-9ec6-6f3333ce7d23"] [17592186110727 :knowledge-point/questions "question-143580a6-1bb7-5c0f-bc9f-072a4a4b0e12"] ["question-4c9070fc-7290-592a-a3f4-9617ce57a8a0" :question/id #uuid "4c9070fc-7290-592a-a3f4-9617ce57a8a0"] ["question-4c9070fc-7290-592a-a3f4-9617ce57a8a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-223686"] ["question-4c9070fc-7290-592a-a3f4-9617ce57a8a0" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(2x+3)(x-k)$ is $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}"] ["question-4c9070fc-7290-592a-a3f4-9617ce57a8a0" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{5}{4},$ we will set our result equal to $\\frac{5}{4}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=(2x+3)(x-k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{3}{2}$ and ${x}_{2}=k.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{2}+k)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{3}{2}+\\frac{2k}{2})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2k-3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{5}{4}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2k-3}{4} & =\\frac{5}{4} \\\\ 2k-3 & =5 \\\\ 2k & =8 \\\\ k & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-4c9070fc-7290-592a-a3f4-9617ce57a8a0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-e93e9559-4f79-5c63-a36b-5702454dc549" :answer-field/id #uuid "e93e9559-4f79-5c63-a36b-5702454dc549"] ["answer-e752a1c1-0510-5a2c-adb0-f4320d6d7556" :answer/id #uuid "e752a1c1-0510-5a2c-adb0-f4320d6d7556"] ["answer-e752a1c1-0510-5a2c-adb0-f4320d6d7556" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-e752a1c1-0510-5a2c-adb0-f4320d6d7556" :answer/value "4"] ["answer-field-e93e9559-4f79-5c63-a36b-5702454dc549" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-e93e9559-4f79-5c63-a36b-5702454dc549" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-e93e9559-4f79-5c63-a36b-5702454dc549" :answer-field/correct "answer-e752a1c1-0510-5a2c-adb0-f4320d6d7556"] ["answer-field-e93e9559-4f79-5c63-a36b-5702454dc549" :answer-field/choices "answer-e752a1c1-0510-5a2c-adb0-f4320d6d7556"] ["question-4c9070fc-7290-592a-a3f4-9617ce57a8a0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-e93e9559-4f79-5c63-a36b-5702454dc549"] [17592186110727 :knowledge-point/questions "question-4c9070fc-7290-592a-a3f4-9617ce57a8a0"] [17592186110978 :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x+5k)(3x-4k)$ is $x=-\\frac{1}{8}.$ Find the value of $k.$\n\n$k=$\n\n{{field-1}}"] [17592186110978 :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{8},$ we will set our result equal to $\\frac{1}{8}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=-(x+5k)(3x-4k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=-5k$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{4k}{3}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-5k+\\frac{4k}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{(-\\frac{11k}{3})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{11k}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{1}{8}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{11k}{6} & =-\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ -11k & =-\\frac{6}{8} \\\\ -11k & =-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ k & =\\frac{3}{44}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186110978 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-663b6d29-5f25-5ddf-b688-280f85dc55f5" :answer/id #uuid "663b6d29-5f25-5ddf-b688-280f85dc55f5"] ["answer-663b6d29-5f25-5ddf-b688-280f85dc55f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-663b6d29-5f25-5ddf-b688-280f85dc55f5" :answer/value "\\frac{3}{44}"] [17592186107606 :answer-field/correct "answer-663b6d29-5f25-5ddf-b688-280f85dc55f5"] [17592186107606 :answer-field/choices "answer-663b6d29-5f25-5ddf-b688-280f85dc55f5"] ["question-04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133" :question/id #uuid "04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133"] ["question-04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133" :question/math-academy-id "q-84911"] ["question-04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of $y=\\frac{1}{3}(k-x)(5x+3k)$ is $x=\\frac{1}{10}.$ The value of $k=$"] ["question-04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{10},$ we will set our result equal to $\\frac{1}{10}.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=\\frac{1}{3}(k-x)(5x+3k),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=k$ and ${x}_{2}=-\\frac{3k}{5}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(k-\\frac{3k}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{5k}{5}-\\frac{3k}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{2k}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{k}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=\\frac{1}{10}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k}{5} & =\\frac{1}{10} \\\\ k & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] ["answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/id #uuid "cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585"] ["answer-193c9dde-df02-57fb-9a38-2e3ada1317a7" :answer/id #uuid "193c9dde-df02-57fb-9a38-2e3ada1317a7"] ["answer-193c9dde-df02-57fb-9a38-2e3ada1317a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-193c9dde-df02-57fb-9a38-2e3ada1317a7" :answer/value "-1"] ["answer-a475de87-e762-598f-af2f-5e440020dd19" :answer/id #uuid "a475de87-e762-598f-af2f-5e440020dd19"] ["answer-a475de87-e762-598f-af2f-5e440020dd19" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-a475de87-e762-598f-af2f-5e440020dd19" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-ff07e237-c85a-5da5-b75b-ecc1a90cc0ca" :answer/id #uuid "ff07e237-c85a-5da5-b75b-ecc1a90cc0ca"] ["answer-ff07e237-c85a-5da5-b75b-ecc1a90cc0ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-ff07e237-c85a-5da5-b75b-ecc1a90cc0ca" :answer/value "1"] ["answer-7f53d534-d2c5-55c9-bc0b-0b43335f20b3" :answer/id #uuid "7f53d534-d2c5-55c9-bc0b-0b43335f20b3"] ["answer-7f53d534-d2c5-55c9-bc0b-0b43335f20b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7f53d534-d2c5-55c9-bc0b-0b43335f20b3" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6" :answer/id #uuid "45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6"] ["answer-45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/correct "answer-45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6"] ["answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/choices "answer-193c9dde-df02-57fb-9a38-2e3ada1317a7"] ["answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/choices "answer-a475de87-e762-598f-af2f-5e440020dd19"] ["answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/choices "answer-ff07e237-c85a-5da5-b75b-ecc1a90cc0ca"] ["answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/choices "answer-7f53d534-d2c5-55c9-bc0b-0b43335f20b3"] ["answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585" :answer-field/choices "answer-45670d3d-36e3-540d-bd5e-bd76637818f6"] ["question-04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-cfed377d-f55c-58f7-a40b-072a8729a585"] [17592186110727 :knowledge-point/questions "question-04b365f6-2d57-5574-aec1-e0a7c1397133"] ["question-d3719257-12a3-5f28-b262-f0a159519b77" :question/id #uuid "d3719257-12a3-5f28-b262-f0a159519b77"] ["question-d3719257-12a3-5f28-b262-f0a159519b77" :question/math-academy-id "q-311977"] ["question-d3719257-12a3-5f28-b262-f0a159519b77" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $22$ | $25$ | $29$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $7$ | $7$ | $1$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}."] ["question-d3719257-12a3-5f28-b262-f0a159519b77" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=22$ and $x=25$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(22)=f(25)=7\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=22$ and $x=25.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabola's vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{22+25}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{47}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-d3719257-12a3-5f28-b262-f0a159519b77" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-20ab70eb-5491-5082-8e0c-fff7c3142ccb" :answer-field/id #uuid "20ab70eb-5491-5082-8e0c-fff7c3142ccb"] ["answer-3dc01742-5f11-5892-91d4-ffa50ff7e871" :answer/id #uuid "3dc01742-5f11-5892-91d4-ffa50ff7e871"] ["answer-3dc01742-5f11-5892-91d4-ffa50ff7e871" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-3dc01742-5f11-5892-91d4-ffa50ff7e871" :answer/value "\\frac{47}{2}"] ["answer-field-20ab70eb-5491-5082-8e0c-fff7c3142ccb" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-20ab70eb-5491-5082-8e0c-fff7c3142ccb" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-20ab70eb-5491-5082-8e0c-fff7c3142ccb" :answer-field/correct "answer-3dc01742-5f11-5892-91d4-ffa50ff7e871"] ["answer-field-20ab70eb-5491-5082-8e0c-fff7c3142ccb" :answer-field/choices "answer-3dc01742-5f11-5892-91d4-ffa50ff7e871"] ["question-d3719257-12a3-5f28-b262-f0a159519b77" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-20ab70eb-5491-5082-8e0c-fff7c3142ccb"] [17592186110728 :knowledge-point/questions "question-d3719257-12a3-5f28-b262-f0a159519b77"] ["question-d2b05f92-b206-55b0-8a81-97fed9a6e7ee" :question/id #uuid "d2b05f92-b206-55b0-8a81-97fed9a6e7ee"] ["question-d2b05f92-b206-55b0-8a81-97fed9a6e7ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-311956"] ["question-d2b05f92-b206-55b0-8a81-97fed9a6e7ee" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $-9$ | $-6$ | $-3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $-10$ | $0$ | $0$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. The parabola opens downward. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}."] ["question-d2b05f92-b206-55b0-8a81-97fed9a6e7ee" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the roots of the parabola are given. They are \n\n$$\nx=-6\\,\\text{and}\\,x=-3.\n$$\n\nIf the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k),$ then by the average of the roots formula, $h$ is simply the average of the two roots. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{-6+(-3)}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{9}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-d2b05f92-b206-55b0-8a81-97fed9a6e7ee" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-19978621-b8ff-589b-9021-591fe866d6ca" :answer-field/id #uuid "19978621-b8ff-589b-9021-591fe866d6ca"] ["answer-dc91623b-454e-5462-b697-e8c2c15d7728" :answer/id #uuid "dc91623b-454e-5462-b697-e8c2c15d7728"] ["answer-dc91623b-454e-5462-b697-e8c2c15d7728" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dc91623b-454e-5462-b697-e8c2c15d7728" :answer/value "-\\frac{9}{2}"] ["answer-field-19978621-b8ff-589b-9021-591fe866d6ca" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-19978621-b8ff-589b-9021-591fe866d6ca" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-19978621-b8ff-589b-9021-591fe866d6ca" :answer-field/correct "answer-dc91623b-454e-5462-b697-e8c2c15d7728"] ["answer-field-19978621-b8ff-589b-9021-591fe866d6ca" :answer-field/choices "answer-dc91623b-454e-5462-b697-e8c2c15d7728"] ["question-d2b05f92-b206-55b0-8a81-97fed9a6e7ee" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-19978621-b8ff-589b-9021-591fe866d6ca"] [17592186110728 :knowledge-point/questions "question-d2b05f92-b206-55b0-8a81-97fed9a6e7ee"] ["question-bac157c9-805d-56d0-9e89-ae7a2f0ad4e6" :question/id #uuid "bac157c9-805d-56d0-9e89-ae7a2f0ad4e6"] ["question-bac157c9-805d-56d0-9e89-ae7a2f0ad4e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-311909"] ["question-bac157c9-805d-56d0-9e89-ae7a2f0ad4e6" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $8$ | $10$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $18$ | $12$ | $12$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}."] ["question-bac157c9-805d-56d0-9e89-ae7a2f0ad4e6" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=10$ and $x=16$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(10)=f(16)=12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=10$ and $x=16.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabola's vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{10+16}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{26}{2} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-bac157c9-805d-56d0-9e89-ae7a2f0ad4e6" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-7345a46e-2929-54cc-8c14-7f0c18a62404" :answer-field/id #uuid "7345a46e-2929-54cc-8c14-7f0c18a62404"] ["answer-cb729667-f5e4-54c6-abc0-13882c8347c3" :answer/id #uuid "cb729667-f5e4-54c6-abc0-13882c8347c3"] ["answer-cb729667-f5e4-54c6-abc0-13882c8347c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-cb729667-f5e4-54c6-abc0-13882c8347c3" :answer/value "13"] ["answer-field-7345a46e-2929-54cc-8c14-7f0c18a62404" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-7345a46e-2929-54cc-8c14-7f0c18a62404" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-7345a46e-2929-54cc-8c14-7f0c18a62404" :answer-field/correct "answer-cb729667-f5e4-54c6-abc0-13882c8347c3"] ["answer-field-7345a46e-2929-54cc-8c14-7f0c18a62404" :answer-field/choices "answer-cb729667-f5e4-54c6-abc0-13882c8347c3"] ["question-bac157c9-805d-56d0-9e89-ae7a2f0ad4e6" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-7345a46e-2929-54cc-8c14-7f0c18a62404"] [17592186110728 :knowledge-point/questions "question-bac157c9-805d-56d0-9e89-ae7a2f0ad4e6"] ["question-29e68a84-4d10-52b0-a908-447f3d997c55" :question/id #uuid "29e68a84-4d10-52b0-a908-447f3d997c55"] ["question-29e68a84-4d10-52b0-a908-447f3d997c55" :question/math-academy-id "q-311952"] ["question-29e68a84-4d10-52b0-a908-447f3d997c55" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $-4$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $0$ | $-12$ | $0$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}."] ["question-29e68a84-4d10-52b0-a908-447f3d997c55" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the roots of the parabola are given. They are \n\n$$\nx=-4\\,\\text{and}\\,x=3.\n$$\n\nIf the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k),$ then by the average of the roots formula, $h$ is simply the average of the two roots. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{-4+3}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-29e68a84-4d10-52b0-a908-447f3d997c55" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-b4b013ca-10cd-512b-b1f4-5961f1844f21" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4b013ca-10cd-512b-b1f4-5961f1844f21"] ["answer-bea0d085-6adf-5a1a-8c0f-b45523b9a881" :answer/id #uuid "bea0d085-6adf-5a1a-8c0f-b45523b9a881"] ["answer-bea0d085-6adf-5a1a-8c0f-b45523b9a881" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-bea0d085-6adf-5a1a-8c0f-b45523b9a881" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}"] ["answer-field-b4b013ca-10cd-512b-b1f4-5961f1844f21" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-b4b013ca-10cd-512b-b1f4-5961f1844f21" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-b4b013ca-10cd-512b-b1f4-5961f1844f21" :answer-field/correct "answer-bea0d085-6adf-5a1a-8c0f-b45523b9a881"] ["answer-field-b4b013ca-10cd-512b-b1f4-5961f1844f21" :answer-field/choices "answer-bea0d085-6adf-5a1a-8c0f-b45523b9a881"] ["question-29e68a84-4d10-52b0-a908-447f3d997c55" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-b4b013ca-10cd-512b-b1f4-5961f1844f21"] [17592186110728 :knowledge-point/questions "question-29e68a84-4d10-52b0-a908-447f3d997c55"] ["question-14e0eb8a-dac7-5f73-9945-6c6e124a2b27" :question/id #uuid "14e0eb8a-dac7-5f73-9945-6c6e124a2b27"] ["question-14e0eb8a-dac7-5f73-9945-6c6e124a2b27" :question/math-academy-id "q-311955"] ["question-14e0eb8a-dac7-5f73-9945-6c6e124a2b27" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $2$ | $4$ | $8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $0$ | $8$ | $0$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y=f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. The parabola opens downward. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?\n\nThe $x$-coordinate of the vertex is\n{{field-1}}."] ["question-14e0eb8a-dac7-5f73-9945-6c6e124a2b27" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the roots of the parabola are given. They are \n\n$$\nx=2\\,\\text{and}\\,x=8.\n$$\n\nIf the coordinates of the vertex are $(h,k),$ then by the average of the roots formula, $h$ is simply the average of the two roots. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{2+8}{2} \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-14e0eb8a-dac7-5f73-9945-6c6e124a2b27" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-97705bf0-0c11-56a9-ac7d-d495a513d0f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "97705bf0-0c11-56a9-ac7d-d495a513d0f7"] ["answer-0b6917b5-0f23-513d-868b-341a9a33bf03" :answer/id #uuid "0b6917b5-0f23-513d-868b-341a9a33bf03"] ["answer-0b6917b5-0f23-513d-868b-341a9a33bf03" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0b6917b5-0f23-513d-868b-341a9a33bf03" :answer/value "5"] ["answer-field-97705bf0-0c11-56a9-ac7d-d495a513d0f7" :answer-field/key "field-1"] ["answer-field-97705bf0-0c11-56a9-ac7d-d495a513d0f7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] ["answer-field-97705bf0-0c11-56a9-ac7d-d495a513d0f7" :answer-field/correct "answer-0b6917b5-0f23-513d-868b-341a9a33bf03"] ["answer-field-97705bf0-0c11-56a9-ac7d-d495a513d0f7" :answer-field/choices "answer-0b6917b5-0f23-513d-868b-341a9a33bf03"] ["question-14e0eb8a-dac7-5f73-9945-6c6e124a2b27" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-97705bf0-0c11-56a9-ac7d-d495a513d0f7"] [17592186110728 :knowledge-point/questions "question-14e0eb8a-dac7-5f73-9945-6c6e124a2b27"]] "retractions" [[17592186110978 :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y = - (x + 5k)(3x - 4k)$ is $x =-\\frac{1}{8}$. Find the value of $k$.$k =$\n{{field-1}}"]]}]